      "content": "that \"nest\" metaphor is pretty spot on. it really does feel like once you clear out one area, you realize there's a whole colony of these redundancies living under the surface. \n\nhow do i keep them from coming back, though? once i've done the initial cleanup, what are some ways to make sure these little pests don't just crawl back into the tables through new entries or bad imports? like, how do i build a permanent \"exterminator\" system into the database itself?",
